Z||000007||Jay||10-21-2001||10:01 AM||||In my opinion I would never go with anything but a Viper alarm.  If you have a professional install it, it will be guarenteed for life.  If you do it yourself (or have someone else do it) you are S.O.L!  Not to put you down or anything Grinthock, but I personally feel it's better to have a autherized dealer do it.  For example, I bought a Viper alarm in Florida, had it installed at Stereo Dimension in Toronto, after six months the remote stopped working.  Donovan simply replaced my remote for free and sent the damaged one back on the spot.  You wouldn't be able to do that if you install it yourself.||||reg||1
